<section class="space--sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-10 text-center">
        <span class="landing-eyebrow">Help</span>
        <h1 class="landing-title">MyDay knowledge base</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">MyDay is more than a journal. It is a system for noticing what matters, preserving small wins, and improving your life with consistent daily practices.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm bg--secondary">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">What MyDay is for</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">The app is designed around three simple ideas:</p>
        <ol class="feature-list feature-list--details">
          <li>
            <strong>Awareness</strong>
            <span>Capture how you feel, what drains you, and what makes your days better.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reflection</strong>
            <span>Record insights and learn from your experiences so you can make smarter choices tomorrow.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Action</strong>
            <span>Connect daily routines to meaningful projects and small, doable tasks.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">Why this matters</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">Life improves when you stop reacting to every impulse and instead build a gentle rhythm of checking in, learning, and choosing what to keep. MyDay supports that rhythm by making it easy to track your wellbeing, remember what helped, and focus on work that feels meaningful.</p>
        <p class="landing-section-text">Use the app to create a habit of recording one thing that went well, one thing that was hard, and one concrete next step you can take.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm bg--secondary">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">How to use MyDay</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">Start with the <%= link_to "Dashboard", dashboards_path %>. It is the place where you set your intention for the day and record your wellbeing signals.</p>
        <ul class="feature-list feature-list--details">
          <li>
            <strong>Set your main task</strong>
            <span>Choose one clear task that will make today feel productive or more meaningful.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Track mood, energy, and alignment</strong>
            <span>These three measurements show whether your day feels good, sustainable, and connected to your purpose.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Log one challenge</strong>
            <span>Capture the most important problem so you can return to it with focus instead of letting it simmer in the background.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Record one lesson</strong>
            <span>The point of reflection is not perfection — it is learning from what actually happened.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Write one gratitude</strong>
            <span>Noticing positive details helps balance your attention and makes progress feel more sustainable.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">Feature reference</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">Each part of the app serves a distinct role. Use the following guide to understand which page to open for each kind of work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mt-4">
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Reflections</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">A space for free-form writing about your day, your emotions, and the context around them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Day Ratings</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Record how aligned your day felt with your values and purpose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Energy</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Track whether you have the energy to sustain your work and other commitments.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Moods</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Capture how you feel and look for patterns across work, rest, and relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Challenges</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Log the biggest thing holding you back so you can focus on solving it instead of ignoring it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Gratitudes</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Practice noticing what is already good in your life, even on hard days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm bg--secondary">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">Projects and work</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">Projects connect the daily habits you track in MyDay to the longer-term work that matters. They help you move from broad goals to clear actions while keeping your ideas and progress in one place.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mt-4">
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Create a project</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Start with a project for any meaningful area of work or growth. It can be a single goal, a study effort, or an ongoing habit you want to support.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Todos</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Break projects into small, achievable tasks. Each todo is a step you can complete, which makes progress feel real and reduces overwhelm.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Time tracker</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Open and close timers for focused work sessions. Tracking time helps you see how long real progress takes and whether your energy is aligned with your priorities.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Posts</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Write project posts to capture progress, insights, or problems. Writing helps you reflect on the work itself, not just the daily feelings around it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Materials</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Keep your notes, references, and study resources organized inside the project they belong to.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-box feature-box--small">
          <h4 class="feature-title">Saved links</h4>
          <p class="feature-text">Save useful links as you find them so you can return to the right information without interrupting your flow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mt-4">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h3 class="landing-section-title">How projects support the daily system</h3>
        <ul class="feature-list feature-list--details">
          <li>
            <strong>Projects give your main task meaning</strong>
            <span>When your daily task lives inside a project, it is easier to connect what you do today to what you want to accomplish over time.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Open todos appear on the dashboard</strong>
            <span>The dashboard surfaces active project work so you can quickly continue what matters most.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Use time tracking to test your assumptions</strong>
            <span>Measuring time shows whether you are spending effort on the right tasks and whether your estimated priorities match reality.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reflect on project progress</strong>
            <span>Project posts and journal entries create a record you can review later, making it easier to spot patterns and refine your strategy.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">Best practices</h2>
        <ul class="feature-list feature-list--details">
          <li>
            <strong>Do this daily.</strong>
            <span>Consistency matters more than perfection. A short check-in every day builds a useful dataset and makes reflection easier.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Focus on small improvements.</strong>
            <span>Choose one small change you can make tomorrow. Over time, small changes compound into better habits.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Review your history.</strong>
            <span>Look back at older entries to see whether your mood, energy, and alignment are improving.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Link your work to meaning.</strong>
            <span>Projects should connect to something you care about. When work feels meaningful, motivation and satisfaction follow.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="space--sm bg--secondary">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="landing-section-title">This page is public</h2>
        <p class="landing-section-text">The help page is available at <strong>/help</strong> for anyone who wants a clear reference about how the app works and why it exists. Use it as your handbook whenever you need a reminder.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
